# PSR-2b — TEMP / ignored-scratch authority unlink

## Goal

Stop **active authority** documents from treating ignored `TEMP/` / `temp/` /
`docs/temp/` trees as fresh-clone truth. Promote the two live companions that
architecture/standards still pointed at; inventory the rest for PSR-2c.

**Not in scope:** deleting TEMP trees, rewriting all phase pack links, committing
the eight deferred dirty docs from PSR-0b.

## Promoted

| From (ignored) | To (tracked) | id | role |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `temp/DENALI_GRAVITY_REMEDIATION_MAP.md` | [`denali-gravity-remediation-map.mdoc`](../../architecture/denali-gravity-remediation-map.mdoc) | `DG-MAP-001` | evidence |
| `temp/platform-surface-cohesion-roadmap.md` | [`platform-surface-cohesion-roadmap.archive.mdoc`](../../standards/platform-surface-cohesion-roadmap.archive.mdoc) | `PSC-ROADMAP-ARCH-001` | archive |

Local ignored copies keep a banner pointer only (not committed).

## Authority gate

```bash
node scripts/ops/psr-2b-no-temp-authority.mjs
```

Hard-fails markdown links / `related_temp` under:

- every `docs/index.yaml` entry
- `docs/architecture/**`
- `docs/standards/**`

## Remaining (deferred to PSR-2c)

Machine inventory:
[`psr-2b-temp-authority-inventory.yaml`](./psr-2b-temp-authority-inventory.yaml)

At capture: **37** phase/dev files still hold markdown links into TEMP/temp.
Those packs are not active index authority; PSR-2c will archive or rewrite them
when phase material moves under `docs/archive/`.

## Exit gate

| Criterion | Result |
| --- | --- |
| Active architecture/standards/index: no ignored-scratch links | Pass (validator) |
| Gravity map + PSC roadmap promoted | Pass |
| TEMP/temp directories not wiped | Pass |
| Deferred dirty docs unstaged | Pass |
| Remaining phase TEMP links inventoried | Pass |

